    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Traces",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 32
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Finding the trace behind a number\n\nEvery span carries a **`correlationId`** \u2014 the same value the API returns in an\nerror body, echoes in the `X-Correlation-Id` response header and writes into\nevery log line. One trace spans the HTTP request, the use case, the SQL\ntransaction and the wallet event that was published afterwards.\n\n**In Grafana** \u2014 *Explore* \u2192 the **Tempo** datasource \u2192 the **TraceQL** tab:\n\n```\n{ .correlationId = \"0199c7cf-1a7c-7d31-9a0e-2ef12d0f6a11\" }\n```\n\nThe same query works on `.transactionId`, `.walletId`, `.providerId`,\n`.messageId` and `.eventId`.\n\n**From a shell**, against the Tempo API published on `localhost:3200`:\n\n```\nmake trace CORRELATION=0199c7cf-1a7c-7d31-9a0e-2ef12d0f6a11\n```\n\n`start` and `end` are not optional there: Tempo searches a default window and\nreturns nothing \u2014 with no error \u2014 for anything outside it. The `make` target\nsupplies the last hour."
      },
      "transparent": false,
      "id": 13
    }
